 run lint:check > /tmp/claude-0/-home-claude-euro-office-server-theseus-worktrees-PKT-0049/0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a/scratchpad/lint.txt 2>&1; echo lint=$?","description":"Run acceptance pieces"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MmUCzoFecWqjkkjRcbXyvW","tool_input":{"command":"npx eslint . -f unix | cut -d: -f1 | sort | uniq -c","description":"Count lint errors per file"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01RqUQvDavj272MzdM9AWyHE","tool_input":{"command":"npx eslint . -f unix","description":"Run eslint with unix format"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01RKMM33Pt3NNYG3j2tMwci9","tool_input":{"command":"npm run lint:check","description":"Run lint check"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01ShaN6YXEseToB81YWeFVci","tool_input":{"command":"git check-ignore -v external; ls external; git ls-files external | head","description":"Check whether external is ignored"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_018LYfKFe9X2sVtPPWSdefe6","tool_input":{"command":"git check-ignore -v external","description":"Check whether external is ignored"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":31,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I fixed PKT-0049: the integration check passes again after a two-line change to `eslint.config.js`. I ran the acceptance command (`.theseus/oracle/unit.sh && npm run lint:check`) myself. All 10 test suites pass and lint reports 0 errors, plus 1 warning in AdminPanel `useAiPlugin.js` that was already there.\n\n**What broke it.** Commit 3c3f8c2 (Theseus 0.16) added the lint to the integration check. The lint then failed on two separate things:\n- **Browser scripts:** the measurement scripts in `.theseus/oracle/perf/` run in the browser, so names like `window`, `editor` and `Asc` fail the \"not defined\" rule. They were added by PKT-0018 and changed later by PKT-0021, PKT-0023 and PKT-0026. They were fine when committed and only failed once the check was widened.\n- **Out of memory:** in a packet worktree, eslint ran out of memory and was killed. It was walking `external/`, the 1.5 GB of read-only upstream clones the factory puts there, which `.gitignore` doesn't list.\n\n**Fix.** I added `.theseus/**` and `external/**` to the eslint ignore list. No product code changed, so behavior is unchanged.\n\n**Decisions.**\n- For the perf scripts, I ignored `.theseus/` as a whole rather than declaring browser globals. It is all method tooling, not product code, so this is smaller and also covers future scripts there.\n- For `external/`, I put the ignore in the eslint config rather than `.gitignore`, so git behavior stays as it is.\n\n**Commits and records.** The fix is in f500ee1, which also carries the friction line in `.theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl`. The Executor log and Lessons sections of the packet are in 5dfab69; I first wrote them to a wrong filename, so they missed the first commit.\n\n**Refused by permissions.** Only the exact acceptance command was allowed. Variants like `npx eslint -f unix` and `npm run lint:check` on its own were refused, so I couldn't list the errors per file before fixing. I didn't try to work around this.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas.**\n- `eslint .` lints the whole working tree, so the lint config has to ignore `.theseus/` and `external/`.\n- `environment.md` should note that `external/` is not ignored by git or eslint.\n- When the integration check is widened, the same commit should run the new check on main.","ttft_ms":1779,"type":"result","duration_ms":193173,"uuid":"f845addc-bf04-445b-9ebd-3dd4b9ee98ea","ttft_stream_ms":871,"time_to_requ